  "scope": "Local macOS arm64; temporary state, actual public QUIC SDK/native audio, actual stateless MCP SDK, protected composition, real provider worker and pinned Vapi SDK against authenticated loopback APIs. No live provider/model operation, public ingress, deployment or production database access.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "requirement": "Expose configured task operations and useful old-source recall to Vapi",
      "tests": [
        "gate4_vapi_call_bootstrap",
        "gate4_vapi_post_call",
        "gate4_provider_tasks",
        "gate4_mcp_recall"
      ],
      "result": "Real MCP discovery and typed calls use a privately verified provider binding. Common bounded recall retrieves a fact beyond the initial context page with source attribution; provider context respects the invocation history ceiling."
    },
    {
      "requirement": "Persist tool results/outcomes and correlate conversation, task, call/session, step and effect",
      "tests": [
        "gate4_vapi_post_call",
        "gate4_vapi_pending_continuation",
        "gate4_vapi_task_voice"
      ],
      "result": "Final native voice sources retain exact journal provenance after restart. The task-bound effect status read returns the persisted question reference; the late reply is explicitly attributed to that question and task. Inbox metadata omits outcome bodies by design."
    },
    {
      "requirement": "Return bounded pending results and recover after host disconnect",
      "tests": [
        "gate4_vapi_pending_continuation",
        "gate4_mcp_deadline"
      ],
      "result": "A controlled slow private SDK request remains pending. A maximum MCP wait returns before ten seconds, with an unchanged empty-page cursor. The host disconnects before provider completion and reconnects to one exact reply and a completed original receipt; no second provider POST or job."
    },
    {
      "requirement": "Route later replies only through the configured task channel under current authority",
      "tests": [
        "gate4_provider_tasks",
        "gate4_reply_recovery",
        "gate4_vapi_recovery_revocation",
        "tasks::tests::effect_provider"
      ],
      "result": "Two tasks sharing one conversation do not wake from each other's provider replies. Cancellation, expiry, revocation, duplicate completion, ambiguous assignment, uncertainty and rollback preserve their existing boundaries. New post-call chat has no call/session/SIP tools."
    },
    {
      "requirement": "Ending voice does not cancel the task; useful post-call continuation survives restart",
      "tests": [
        "gate4_vapi_post_call",
        "gate4_vapi_task_voice",
        "tasks::tests::media_context"
      ],
      "result": "Voice ends with a retained decision. The owned server restarts against its existing database; the original task remains Waiting in the original conversation. An explicit human reply affects only that task. A fresh chat invocation recalls the unchanged decision and new reply, derives a follow-up from those returned bodies and creates one message on replay without another call."
    },
    {
      "requirement": "Completed, denied and pending outcomes preserve provenance and current access",
      "tests": [
        "gate4_vapi_pending_continuation",
        "gate4_mcp_retention",
        "gate4_vapi_voice_revocation",
        "gate4_vapi_bootstrap_recovery"
      ],
      "result": "An invalid business send records one failed effect without sending; matching failure replay preserves the snapshot. An uncertain creation retains its original intent rather than retrying a POST. Expired artifact bytes and revoked context remain unavailable; retained source references remain explicit."
    }
  ],
